        "original_id": "ec7aeade-994d-51a7-b662-6de532739c31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Danny Bonaduce, Joseph Bonaduce, Bonnie Franklin, Mackenzie Phillips, Valerie Bertinelli, Cheyenne Haynes\n- TV Shows: One Day at a Time, I Know My Kid's a Star, The Partridge Family\n- Networks: CBS, Lifetime Movie Network\n- Places: Broomall, Pennsylvania, Indianapolis\n- Roles: host, primary judge, child actor, TV writer, producer, comedian, professional wrestler, radio/television personality\n\nFacts:\n- One Day at a Time is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from December 16, 1975, until May 28, 1984.\n- One Day at a Time starred Bonnie Franklin as a divorced mother raising two teenage daughters in Indianapolis, and Mackenzie Phillips and Valerie Bertinelli played the daughters.\n- Danny Bonaduce was born on August 13, 1959, in Broomall, Pennsylvania.\n- Danny Bonaduce is an American radio and television personality, comedian, professional wrestler, and former child actor.\n- Danny Bonaduce is the son of veteran TV writer and producer Joseph Bonaduce, who worked on The Dick Van Dyke Show and One Day at a Time.\n- Danny Bonaduce is best known for being a child actor on the 1970s TV show The Partridge Family.\n- I Know My Kid's a Star featured Danny Bonaduce as its host and primary judge.\n- Cheyenne Haynes is known for the Lifetime Movie Network television film Lies in Plain Sight and for I Know My Kid's a Star.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
